---

# Understanding the Query

The numerator

```promql
container_memory_working_set_bytes
```

represents the amount of memory actively being used by the container.

Unlike total allocated memory,

this excludes reclaimable cache and focuses on the working set.

---

The denominator

```promql
container_spec_memory_limit_bytes
```

represents the maximum amount of memory the container is allowed to consume.

---

The query therefore calculates:

```

Current Memory Usage

———————————————

Maximum Memory Limit

```

which produces a value between

```

0

and

1

```

Example

```

Memory Used

512 MB

Memory Limit

1024 MB

Result

0.50

=

50%

```

---

# Why Use sum()

The Enterprise Platform may eventually run multiple replicas.

Each Pod exposes its own container metrics.

Using

```promql
sum(...)
/
sum(...)
```

calculates the percentage across all Pods,

providing a platform-wide view of memory utilization.

